<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/confidenceScore> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Degree of belief, between 0 and 1, that the asserted value is correct: 1 = certain, 0.5 = undecided, 0 = believed false. The assessor is either the agent the assertion is attributed to (prov:wasAttributedTo) or the activity that generated the assertion (prov:wasGeneratedBy), e.g. an extraction that codes how firmly the source states the claim; hg:confidenceMethod says which, and by what rubric. Scores are comparable only when they share an assessor or a method."@en .
