<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/epochDateGregorian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Proleptic Gregorian (ISO 8601, astronomical year numbering) date on which the era began, in the era's own reckoning (Bikram Sambat counts from year 1, e.g. -0056-04-14, a nominal back-projection of the modern solar reckoning rather than an attested date; Nepal Sambat counts elapsed years from year 0, 0879-10-24 = 20 October 879 Julian). Its month and day only indicate the approximate new-year season: the actual new year varies (Bikram Sambat 13-15 April, solar; Nepal Sambat late October to November, lunisolar), so it must not be used for day-level conversion. A value ending in -01-01 marks a calendar whose new year is 1 January, for which year conversion is exact."@en .
